  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 230 PM Tuesday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Unsettled weather and near to above normal rainfall \nare expected late this week into the weekend.\n\n\ufeffThe stalled frontal boundary to our south will gradually lift north \nacross the region by Thursday, accelerating a warming and moistening \ntrend. Meanwhile, a series of shortwave troughs tracking through the \nMidwest will carve out a broader upper-level trough over the eastern \nU.S. This pattern evolution will result in an unsettled weather from \nThursday through the weekend.\n\nPrecipitation coverage will likely peak Friday into Saturday as PW \nvalues surge toward 2.0 inches, coinciding with a final, amplifying \nshortwave digging into the Tennessee Valley and southern \nAppalachians along with a surface cold front. While widespread cloud \ncover and daily convective overturning may limit diurnal \ndestabilization, deep southwesterly flow and modest instability will \nsupport scattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms. Cumulative \nrainfall is expected to be near or above normal, with an outside \nthreat of localized flooding based on the pattern.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... Heat is expected to return next week.\n\nThe frontal zone should again stall to our south over the weekend, \nwith a gradual pattern shift expected into next week as upper level \nheights build across the Deep South. \n\nDiscrepancies exist in the extended guidance regarding the amplitude \nof this transition:\n\nGFS-based guidance favors strong, anomalous ridging over the eastern \nU.S. by mid-to-late week.\n\nECMWF-based guidance depicts flatter, more zonal flow initially, \nfollowed by and expanding ridge late in the period.\n\nRegardless of the exact model solution, both global models support a \nrobust warming trend. Temperatures are expected to climb well above \nnormal (climo highs are mid to upper 80s) by late next week, \naccompanied by a return to a typical summertime pattern featuring \nisolated/scattered showers and storms and near-normal precipitation.",
